    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116122" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠκῠ-πέτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>swift-flying, swift-running,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππω ὠκυπέτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.42
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				13.24
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴρηξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					212
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠ. μόρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1042
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.):—also fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠκυπέτη</span></b> , name of a Harpy, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				267
			</span></i>; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠκυπέτεια</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χελιδών,</span> of a fish (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χελιδών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Marc.Sid.
				17
			</span></i>.</div>
